 "about": "Estimates energy and protein of a restaurant or delivery dish that has no nutrition label (Wolt, foodora and daily menus publish none, 19/10/2026). A dish is matched by its Czech or English words (a rule word must START a word of the dish name: 'krut' matches 'krůtí' but not 'krutonky'; a word ending in a space must be the whole word) to a dish TYPE; a type is a mix of COMPONENTS in grams for one usual portion; every component's values per 100 g come from USDA FoodData Central, Food and Nutrient Database for Dietary Studies (FNDDS), read 19/10/2026 at https://fdc.nal.usda.gov/food-details/<fdc>/nutrients. The weight on the menu scales the whole mix; a daily-menu weight such as '150g Španělský ptáček' is the MEAT weight (Czech custom) and sets only the first component. Everything this file produces is labelled 'estimate'. Used by tools/dine.py and, for the shortlist only, by tools/browser/dish-core.js (same rules; tests/t_dine.py proves they agree).",
 "source": "U.S. Department of Agriculture, Agricultural Research Service. (2024). FoodData Central: Food and Nutrient Database for Dietary Studies 2021-2023. https://fdc.nal.usda.gov/",
