 "fallback_type": "grill",
 "fallback_note": "No dish word but a meat or fish word in the NAME (for example \"Krokety z vepřového masa\"): counted as type grill (meat + side).",
 "min_meal_price": 80,
 "meat_weight_min": 60,
 "count_note": "A count in the name (\"8x BBQ Wings\", \"6 ks\", \"1ks\") with a type that has piece_g gives the weight: 8 x 30 g.",
 "weight_rules": "1) the weight field of the menu (Wolt unit_info) = whole dish; 2) grams at the START of the name or description (\"100g Grilované kuřecí medailonky\") = meat weight (Czech menu custom), also every daily-menu weight, EXCEPT for types marked lead_g \"dish\" (pasta, gnocchi, risotto, noodles, salads, bowls ...), where grams of lead_dish_g_min (200 g) or more are the whole dish (\"250g Tagliatelle s kuřecím masem\") and fewer stay the meat (\"100g Těstoviny s krůtími prsy\"); 3) grams elsewhere in the name or description = whole dish; 4) a count with piece_g; 5) else the type default portion. A whole dish under weight_g_min is a snack (refused); without any weight, a price under min_meal_price (80 CZK) is a side, sauce or kids portion (refused).",
 "changes": [
  "2026-10-19 S4 first live Wolt read (Blanice kolej): price floor 60 -> 80 CZK (sauces, soy-sauce bowl 10 CZK, plain noodles 50-60 CZK counted as meals); sashimi, tatarák, miso, kids menus, sauce sets refused; meat-free burgers refused (no table value); cheese fingers = fried cheese 25 g a piece.",
  "2026-10-19 S4: leading grams are the whole dish for one-pot types (lead_g dish); \"250g Tagliatelle s kuřecím masem\" had been read as 250 g of chicken.",
  "2026-10-19 S4 run 1: KFC \"Kyblík 30 Hot Wings\" (a sharing bucket, 900 g) refused: kyblík, bucket.",
  "2026-10-19 S4 run 1: foodora lists a dish whose size is chosen later at 1 CZK (K-Bang \"Classic Wings 1 CZK, 6/8/12ks\"): any price under 30 CZK is a placeholder, refused.",
  "2026-10-19 S4 run 1: foodora \"Steakové hranolky\" (steak fries) and \"Americké brambory, křupavé...\" (crispy potatoes) were planned as 50 g protein meals: \"krupav\" alone no longer means breaded chicken, steak fries refused, and a dish whose name STARTS with a side word (brambory, hranolky, rýže...) with no meat word in the name is a side, refused.",
  "2026-10-19 S4 run 1: Wolt \"BRODO DI MANZO\" (beef broth, described \"hovězí vývar s masem ... nudle\") was planned as a meal through the meat-and-side-in-the-description rule: that rule now needs no soup word in the description (soup_words), and brodo is refused.",
  "2026-10-19 S4 run 2 (Eat out, Chodov): \"Pizza Pane\" (pizza-dough garlic bread) counted as a 450 g pizza, and \"Curry rýže\" / \"Tikka N rice\" (sauce and rice, no meat named) counted with 130 g chicken: pizza bread refused; curry and bowl without a meat word now have no meat (default_protein none).",
  "2026-10-19 S4 independent review: a small weight on a meat-led dish (\"Kuřecí řízek 150g\", \"Hovězí steak 200 g\") is now the meat weight (meat_led_types, 300 g), not the whole dish (protein was 2-3 times too low); more than 16 pieces, \"pro 2/4 osoby\", kids portions (\"pro děti\") and half portions (\"1/2 porce\", \"poloviční\") are refused; a salad with no meat, fish, cheese or tofu is a side; weights are read with ASCII digits only and every Unicode space read as a space, the same in Python and JS; allergens: the 14 EU allergens by name and menu number (allergens)."
 ],
